WEBVTT

1
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.909
<i>NARRATOR: Long ago, a mythic</i>
<i>battle between good and evil</i>

2
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.673
<i>played out in ancient China.</i>

3
00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.194
<i>The country was torn by civil war,</i>

4
00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.352
<i>with many kingdoms</i>
<i>struggling for land and power.</i>

5
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:57.431
<i>But one king had a ruthless ambition</i>
<i>to make himself emperor by the sword.</i>

6
00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:07.508
(CLEARING THROAT)

7
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:19.869
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

8
00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.188
Leave me.

9
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:23.316
Prepare for war!

10
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.192
<i>NARRATOR: The other rulers hired assassins</i>
<i>to kill the King</i>

11
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.794
<i>before he could conquer them all.</i>

12
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.275
(GRUNTING)

13
00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.236
(SWORDS CLASHING)

14
00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:04.669
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

15
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.272
Stop! I am not harmed.

16
00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:18.869
We attack tonight!

17
00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.075
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

18
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:36.431
<i>NARRATOR: Kingdom by kingdom,</i>
<i>his army swept away everything in its path,</i>

19
00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:40.195
<i>and anyone who resisted met a terrible fate.</i>

20
00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.918
<i>The country was his.</i>

21
00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:48.037
<i>He was now Emperor of All Under Heaven.</i>

22
00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:54.191
<i>He enslaved his conquered enemies</i>
<i>and forced them to build his Great Wall.</i>

23
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.034
<i>When they were dead or useless,</i>
<i>he had them buried beneath it.</i>

24
00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:32.119
<i>The Emperor's mystics taught him</i>
<i>mastery over the five elements,</i>

25
00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.988
<i>fire, water, earth, wood and metal.</i>

26
00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.310
<i>His power seemed without limit.</i>

27
00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.476
<i>He was master of millions,</i>

28
00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.189
<i>but like the lowliest peasant,</i>
<i>he could not stop growing old.</i>

29
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.269
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

30
00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.273
I have too much to do for one lifetime.

31
00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:58.274
<i>NARRATOR: He needed to defeat</i>
<i>his last enemy, death itself.</i>

32
00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.432
<i>One day, news came of a powerful witch</i>

33
00:04:08.520 --> 00:04:11.910
<i>who was rumoured to know</i>
<i>the secret to eternal life.</i>

34
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:17.028
<i>He ordered General Ming, his oldest friend</i>
<i>and trusted ally, to find her.</i>

35
00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.150
<i>The witch was named Zi Yuan,</i>

36
00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:33.277
<i>and she was nothing</i>
<i>like the General expected.</i>

37
00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.229
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

38
00:04:42.320 --> 00:04:43.514
Your Majesty...

39
00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:49.989
Rise up.

40
00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:56.556
I do not possess the secret of
immortality, my Lord...

41
00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.473
...but I know where to find it.

42
00:05:00.880 --> 00:05:01.869
General...

43
00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:06.038
No man is to touch her.

44
00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:09.750
She is mine.

45
00:05:14.600 --> 00:05:18.229
<i>NARRATOR: On the western border</i>
<i>stood the Monastery of Turfan.</i>

46
00:05:18.320 --> 00:05:22.154
<i>There was housed the greatest library</i>
<i>in the ancient world,</i>

47
00:05:22.240 --> 00:05:26.279
<i>and Zi Yuan was sure</i>
<i>the secret to eternal life was here.</i>

48
00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:49.109
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

49
00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:51.031
This is a key.

50
00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:02.399
<i>NARRATOR: It was the long lost</i>
<i>oracle bones,</i>

51
00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:06.632
<i>a collection of all the mystical secrets</i>
<i>of the ancient world.</i>

52
00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:12.033
<i>The Emperor's answer was here</i>
<i>along with other magic beyond imagining.</i>

53
00:06:21.720 --> 00:06:22.709
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

54
00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:24.597
You have served me well.

55
00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:30.192
I will grant you anything you desire.

56
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:35.115
I want to spend my life with General Ming.

57
00:06:37.360 --> 00:06:38.793
Of course.

58
00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:40.349
Read.

59
00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:48.873
(CHANTING IN SANSKRIT)

60
00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.390
<i>NARRATOR: She cast the spell in Sanskrit,</i>

61
00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:03.359
<i>an ancient language</i>
<i>that the Emperor did not understand.</i>

62
00:07:07.800 --> 00:07:08.789
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

63
00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:11.189
I feel your spell working.

64
00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:18.158
I am now immortal.

65
00:07:19.560 --> 00:07:22.233
Come, I want to show you something.

66
00:07:34.080 --> 00:07:35.433
(EXCLAIMING)

67
00:07:37.240 --> 00:07:40.755
Become my queen and I will let him live.

68
00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:44.795
Do what he says! Save yourself!

69
00:07:48.640 --> 00:07:50.835
You will never keep your word.

70
00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.389
You are right.

71
00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:01.273
(GRUNTING)

72
00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.229
(GASPS)

73
00:08:06.760 --> 00:08:08.751
Now, join General Ming in hell.

74
00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:24.671
(SHOUTING)

75
00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:26.034
What did you do to me?

76
00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:29.036
I cursed you and your army.

77
00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:42.199
(EMPEROR GRUNTING IN PAIN)

78
00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:44.519
Surround the Palace!

79
00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:45.993
The Emperor is in trouble!

80
00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:04.190
<i>NARRATOR: The curse must never be lifted,</i>

81
00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:08.592
<i>or the Emperor will rise again</i>
<i>to enslave all of mankind.</i>

82
00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:13.310
<i>On that dark day,</i>
<i>there will be nothing and no one to save us.</i>

83
00:09:27.320 --> 00:09:30.118
You can run, but you can't hide.

84
00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:37.629
One o'clock.

85
00:09:37.720 --> 00:09:39.358
OXFORDSHIRE, ENGLAND

86
00:09:40.280 --> 00:09:44.910
Ten o'clock, one o'clock. Ten o'clock, one...

87
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.798
And this is something for grown men to do?

88
00:09:49.400 --> 00:09:52.119
(EXCLAIMING IN PAIN)

89
00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:57.914
(GRUNTING) Come on.

90
00:10:01.840 --> 00:10:03.159
(SCREAMS)

91
00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:07.833
Bite on this.

92
00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.756
Evy, I'm home!

93
00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:29.752
Mrs O'Connell is at her book reading, sir.
She'll be home for dinner.

94
00:10:29.840 --> 00:10:33.435
Oh, right. Well, that's great,
'cause we're having fish.

95
00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:38.238
You didn't think I'd catch anything,
did you?

96
00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.754
I had the utmost confidence, sir.

97
00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:47.356
JAMESON: There's a hook in your neck, sir.
Shall I fetch the wire cutters?

98
00:10:52.120 --> 00:10:56.989
<i>RICK: Fall back! Follow me!</i>
<i>Move! Move! Move! Move!</i>

99
00:11:01.360 --> 00:11:03.635
<i>EVELYN: "Now safely aboard the airship</i>
<i>with the mummy finally vanquished,</i>

100
00:11:03.720 --> 00:11:04.755
LONDON

101
00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.149
<i>"Dash swept Scarlet into his arms.</i>

102
00:11:08.400 --> 00:11:13.315
"'Oh, God, Scarlet, I thought I'd lost you.'
'For a moment there, you did.'

103
00:11:13.880 --> 00:11:16.474
"Bathed in rays of golden sunlight,

104
00:11:16.560 --> 00:11:21.429
"our heroes sealed their reunion
with a kiss of timeless passion,

105
00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:24.910
"their love deeper and truer than ever."

106
00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:33.515
Mrs O'Connell, we're all dying to know,

107
00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.956
is the Scarlet O'Keefe character
really based on you?

108
00:11:38.480 --> 00:11:41.677
Honestly, I can say
she's a completely different person.

109
00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.671
- Any more questions?
- WOMAN: Mrs O'Connell...

110
00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:48.117
Mrs O'Connell, is your life today
as exciting as it was before the war?

111
00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:49.789
(SIGHS)

112
00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:51.836
I wish my life were that exciting now.

113
00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:53.273
MAN: Will there be another book
in the series?

114
00:11:53.360 --> 00:11:55.828
WOMAN 2: Do you believe in happy endings?

115
00:11:56.960 --> 00:11:57.949
(EXHALES)

116
00:11:58.800 --> 00:12:00.791
Isn't this blissful?

117
00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:04.632
Dinner at home.

118
00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:08.196
- Every night.
- Every night.

119
00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:12.629
- Here's to retirement.
- May we stay this happy forever.

120
00:12:16.640 --> 00:12:17.629
(GULPS)

121
00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:29.514
Still no letter from Alex.
I've sent him three in the last month.

122
00:12:29.600 --> 00:12:30.715
Yeah, well, what do you expect?

123
00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:31.869
The only time we ever hear from that kid

124
00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:34.076
is when he's getting kicked out of college
or he needs more money.

125
00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:37.072
I'm sure he's just buried in his studies.

126
00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:47.199
- So, how did your book reading go?
- Oh, fine. Thank you.

127
00:12:48.040 --> 00:12:50.918
Until they asked me, "When will there
be another Mummy adventure?"

128
00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:53.434
Yeah, but you did promise the publisher
a third book.

129
00:12:53.520 --> 00:12:54.555
I know.

130
00:12:54.640 --> 00:12:58.792
But I spend my nights staring
at a blank page, completely blocked.

131
00:12:58.880 --> 00:13:03.829
We could skip dinner, and I could

132
00:13:03.920 --> 00:13:08.994
attempt to inspire you upstairs.

133
00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:12.751
Oh, that's so sweet of you, darling.

134
00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:17.277
But I'm going to sit at that typewriter
until something exciting comes out.

135
00:13:19.240 --> 00:13:20.832
Thank you.

136
00:13:22.720 --> 00:13:23.709
(EXCLAIMING DELIGHTEDLY)

137
00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.438
Trout. How lovely!

138
00:13:25.520 --> 00:13:26.555
(JAMESON CLEARS THROAT)

139
00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.635
I'm so happy you found a hobby
that doesn't involve guns.

140
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:34.989
(CRUNCHING)

141
00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:42.717
NINGXIA PROVINCE, CHINA

142
00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:53.909
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

143
00:13:54.000 --> 00:13:55.399
Don't worry, we'll find the entrance today.

144
00:13:56.640 --> 00:13:59.313
Li Tung, what's for lunch?

145
00:13:59.400 --> 00:14:00.389
Noodle soup.

146
00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.153
Very good.

147
00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:09.996
ALEX: Good. Wilson's back.

148
00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:13.510
You're a couple days late, Professor.

149
00:14:13.600 --> 00:14:15.033
I was beginning to think
you'd run into bandits.

150
00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:17.031
Oh, my dear fellow,
thank you for the concern.

151
00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.758
- Are you thirsty?
- Oh, yes, please.

152
00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:20.796
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

153
00:14:21.920 --> 00:14:23.876
You know,
when I saw you standing up there,

154
00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.030
I thought I was looking at your father.

155
00:14:26.120 --> 00:14:27.792
You really are Rick O'Connell's son.

156
00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:32.510
Yeah, well, hopefully after today,
he'll be known as Alex O'Connell's father.

157
00:14:32.600 --> 00:14:35.194
What a powerful face!

158
00:14:35.280 --> 00:14:39.068
When I told my colleagues at the museum
that you had discovered the Colossus,

159
00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:40.675
they were thrilled.

160
00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:42.876
- Yes, however...
- I know.

161
00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:44.951
When am I gonna get in that tomb?

162
00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.996
Don't let the buggers get you down.

163
00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.389
It was you that discovered
the Bembridge journal,

164
00:14:49.480 --> 00:14:51.869
and with it, you'll discover the Emperor.

165
00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:55.555
- I have complete faith in you, Alex.
- Thank you, Professor.

166
00:14:56.200 --> 00:14:57.872
Thanks for believing in me.

167
00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:58.949
(MAN SHOUTS)

168
00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.912
We found it! We found the door!

169
00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.792
<i>Bad Mummy.</i>

170
00:15:08.280 --> 00:15:09.599
Yeah.

171
00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:12.911
<i>Vile Mummy?</i>

172
00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:14.429
(TYPING)

173
00:15:15.240 --> 00:15:16.514
No. <i>Cursed Mummy!</i>

174
00:15:16.800 --> 00:15:19.394
<i>Mysterious Mummy.</i>

175
00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.590
<i>Malignant Mummy.</i>

176
00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:29.791
Prepare to die!

177
00:15:31.440 --> 00:15:32.873
Take that!

178
00:15:40.960 --> 00:15:42.188
Rick!

179
00:15:43.960 --> 00:15:45.837
Darling, where are you?

180
00:15:56.040 --> 00:15:58.190
I'm ready to be inspired.

181
00:16:04.680 --> 00:16:08.514
Do you remember the time
the mummy had me tied down?

182
00:16:08.600 --> 00:16:12.388
And you came to save me and you cut...

183
00:16:12.480 --> 00:16:16.553
No! You tore open the ropes
is what you did,

184
00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:19.359
just as he was about to plunge his...

185
00:16:19.440 --> 00:16:21.795
(SNORING)

186
00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:23.239
Oh, rats.

187
00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.109
(LAUGHS)

188
00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:51.199
Watch out!

189
00:16:57.880 --> 00:17:00.269
- Emperor didn't want any houseguests.
- Yeah.

190
00:17:00.360 --> 00:17:01.395
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

191
00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:02.469
Stay together.

192
00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:28.717
Sir Colin Bembridge.

193
00:17:29.480 --> 00:17:30.879
Oh, gee...

194
00:17:31.680 --> 00:17:33.955
He went searching for this tomb
70 years ago.

195
00:17:34.040 --> 00:17:35.917
They left him like this as a warning.

196
00:17:36.000 --> 00:17:38.673
Unfortunately, this is not the dead man
that's gonna make us famous.

197
00:17:38.760 --> 00:17:40.432
Let's keep moving.

198
00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:17.073
Look at it, Alex.

199
00:18:18.080 --> 00:18:19.593
Look at it!

200
00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.670
(SCREAMING)

201
00:18:56.760 --> 00:18:58.159
Chu Wah!

202
00:18:58.240 --> 00:19:00.879
(WHIMPERING)

203
00:19:08.560 --> 00:19:10.152
(SHOUTS IN MANDARIN)

204
00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:38.472
(PANTING)

205
00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:41.512
- Chu Wah.
- No, no, don't, don't, don't.

206
00:19:41.600 --> 00:19:44.194
Alex, Alex, they're dead! Come on.

207
00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:47.272
This kind of danger goes with the territory.
You know that better than anyone.

208
00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:48.588
Alex!

209
00:19:52.720 --> 00:19:54.233
- Yes?
- Okay.

210
00:19:54.320 --> 00:19:55.673
- Yes?
- Yeah.

211
00:19:56.320 --> 00:20:00.677
All right, good chap. Okay. Good chap.
Oh, Jesus.

212
00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.916
All the warriors are facing in to this point,

213
00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:12.197
- as if awaiting an order from the Emperor.
- Well, then, where is he?

214
00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:16.671
Listen, you don't think some bloody grave
robber's beaten us to the prize, do you?

215
00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:18.398
No, he's still here.

216
00:20:18.480 --> 00:20:21.552
You see, this is a feng shui compass.

217
00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.874
Okay. Now. This...

218
00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.791
Okay, this is true north,

219
00:20:33.880 --> 00:20:37.953
but the feng shui compass
is set in the opposite direction.

220
00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:40.031
- All right, we need to realign it.
- All right.

221
00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:42.111
- All right, here we go.
- All right.

222
00:20:51.760 --> 00:20:53.239
(ALEX SCREAMS)

223
00:21:00.320 --> 00:21:03.153
(RAT SQUEAKING)

224
00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:06.076
Alex! Alex, speak to me!

225
00:21:06.560 --> 00:21:08.232
Are you all right?

226
00:21:09.360 --> 00:21:11.749
- Alex!
- I'm fine.

227
00:21:12.840 --> 00:21:15.308
Tell me, have we found the Emperor?

228
00:21:19.000 --> 00:21:20.194
Alex!

229
00:21:27.680 --> 00:21:28.874
What is it?

230
00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:31.793
It's only the greatest find since King Tut!

231
00:21:35.440 --> 00:21:39.274
"If he is awakened,
all mortals should despair."

232
00:21:39.360 --> 00:21:41.237
It's definitely him!

233
00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:45.199
(ALEX EXCLAIMS)

234
00:21:45.360 --> 00:21:47.715
Even had his concubines buried alive
with him.

235
00:21:47.800 --> 00:21:49.119
Selfish bastard.

236
00:21:49.720 --> 00:21:52.712
Hey, Professor Wilson,
you want to come down and take a look?

237
00:21:52.800 --> 00:21:55.837
Or are you so overwhelmed you can't talk?

238
00:21:58.000 --> 00:21:58.989
(THUD)

239
00:22:02.160 --> 00:22:05.232
(GRUNTING)

240
00:22:18.800 --> 00:22:20.119
Wilson!

241
00:22:46.480 --> 00:22:48.152
(PANTING)

242
00:23:28.200 --> 00:23:31.317
Let's go, Professor.
We've got a lot of work to do.

243
00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:32.276
WILSON: All right.

244
00:23:38.200 --> 00:23:39.758
FRY: First of all, I'd just like to say

245
00:23:39.840 --> 00:23:42.957
that the Foreign Office appreciates
all that you did during the war.

246
00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:47.192
But I've been sent to offer you
one last assignment.

247
00:23:47.880 --> 00:23:52.078
I'm afraid we've retired
from the espionage game, haven't we, dear?

248
00:23:52.160 --> 00:23:54.230
Yeah, we've... We don't do that any more.
We're finished.

249
00:23:54.320 --> 00:23:56.550
- EVELYN: Not at all.
- Completely done.

250
00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:01.597
But just out of curiosity,
what is the mission anyway?

251
00:24:01.680 --> 00:24:04.877
We need you to courier this to Shanghai.

252
00:24:06.560 --> 00:24:07.549
(EVELYN GASPS)

253
00:24:08.200 --> 00:24:11.431
- Nice piece of ice.
- It's the Eye of Shangri-La.

254
00:24:11.520 --> 00:24:14.876
If you believe the legend,
it points the way to the Pool of Eternal Life.

255
00:24:14.960 --> 00:24:17.030
It was smuggled out of China in 1940.

256
00:24:17.120 --> 00:24:19.759
Now, the government would like
to return it to the Shanghai Museum

257
00:24:19.840 --> 00:24:23.116
as a sign of good faith
to the Chinese people.

258
00:24:23.200 --> 00:24:26.954
And with your expertise in the field,
we naturally thought of you.

259
00:24:27.040 --> 00:24:29.838
Oh, we'd be so flattered.

260
00:24:31.840 --> 00:24:35.515
But Rick and I, we made a promise
to each other after the war

261
00:24:35.600 --> 00:24:38.558
that we would settle down.

262
00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:41.359
- That's right, yeah, we did, didn't we? We...
- I see.

263
00:24:41.440 --> 00:24:44.238
Well, I must admit I am a little disappointed.

264
00:24:44.320 --> 00:24:47.596
Postwar China is very dangerous.

265
00:24:47.680 --> 00:24:52.390
There are a lot of factions that would love
to get their hands on the Eye of Shangri-La.

266
00:24:52.480 --> 00:24:55.950
In lesser hands,
the Eye could be lost forever.

267
00:24:56.720 --> 00:24:58.312
We couldn't let that happen, could we?

268
00:24:58.400 --> 00:25:00.709
No, that could be bad for the world.

269
00:25:00.800 --> 00:25:02.870
- The world... Terrible.
- Yeah.

270
00:25:03.920 --> 00:25:05.433
You know, she has a brother
who lives in Shanghai.

271
00:25:05.520 --> 00:25:07.272
- Jonathan!
- Yes.

272
00:25:07.360 --> 00:25:09.157
He owns a nightclub, if I'm not mistaken.

273
00:25:09.240 --> 00:25:10.639
We have been meaning to visit. We could...

274
00:25:10.720 --> 00:25:11.948
- We should...
...drop in and surprise him.

275
00:25:12.040 --> 00:25:13.632
- Say hello.
- Why not?

276
00:25:13.720 --> 00:25:16.871
Does this mean
we can count on you one last time?

277
00:25:18.160 --> 00:25:19.149
Yes.

278
00:25:22.680 --> 00:25:24.352
SHANGHAI, CHINA

279
00:25:24.440 --> 00:25:26.317
CHINESE NEW YEAR, 1947

280
00:25:32.280 --> 00:25:33.872
(CAR HONKING)

281
00:25:36.560 --> 00:25:38.391
(MUSIC PLAYING)

282
00:25:48.240 --> 00:25:50.674
(PEOPLE CHATTERING)

283
00:25:52.080 --> 00:25:53.229
There we are.

284
00:25:54.840 --> 00:25:56.876
Here's to you, Princess.

285
00:25:56.960 --> 00:26:00.077
And Imhotep.
May the bugger actually stay dead.

286
00:26:00.160 --> 00:26:01.195
(TOASTING IN RUSSIAN)

287
00:26:01.280 --> 00:26:02.633
Ding-dong.

288
00:26:10.440 --> 00:26:12.795
Hi, can you buy a drink for me?

289
00:26:13.640 --> 00:26:16.438
Excuse me. Alex! Alex! You're back again.

290
00:26:16.520 --> 00:26:17.919
Come here, Alex. Let me get you a drink.

291
00:26:18.000 --> 00:26:20.389
Smooth special for the pup, huh?
The explorer.

292
00:26:20.640 --> 00:26:21.629
(LAUGHS)

293
00:26:22.480 --> 00:26:23.799
Make that two.

294
00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:26.314
Sorry, Uncle Jon, but I got a better offer.

295
00:26:26.400 --> 00:26:29.949
JONATHAN: No, no, Alex. No, look.
Listen, how can I... Come here.

296
00:26:30.040 --> 00:26:31.758
To put it in archaeological terms,

297
00:26:31.840 --> 00:26:33.956
that's a tomb
in which many pharaohs have lain.

298
00:26:34.040 --> 00:26:36.838
Now, listen, listen,
just think about me for a moment, all right?

299
00:26:36.920 --> 00:26:40.549
Your discovery will go public in a few days,
and your parents are sure to find out.

300
00:26:40.640 --> 00:26:43.074
They're not gonna be happy
you've dropped out of school. And...

301
00:26:43.160 --> 00:26:46.835
Will you relax, Uncle Jon? Okay? I'm here.
They're a long way away.

302
00:26:46.920 --> 00:26:49.639
- Alex...
- Excuse me, okay?

303
00:26:49.720 --> 00:26:51.915
I have some excavation to do.

304
00:26:59.720 --> 00:27:01.039
Jonathan!

305
00:27:03.480 --> 00:27:05.038
(LAUGHS NERVOUSLY)

306
00:27:05.120 --> 00:27:08.157
You're in China! Evy. Rick.

307
00:27:08.240 --> 00:27:10.515
(STUTTERING) What are you... It's so...
I didn't even...

308
00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:13.672
Brother, how lovely to see you.

309
00:27:13.760 --> 00:27:15.432
I had no idea he was here!

310
00:27:15.520 --> 00:27:16.919
- Who was here?
- Who?

311
00:27:17.680 --> 00:27:18.715
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

312
00:27:18.800 --> 00:27:20.791
MAN: This happens every time!

313
00:27:21.680 --> 00:27:23.750
Every man in the bar!

314
00:27:23.840 --> 00:27:24.875
- Dad?
- Alex!

315
00:27:24.960 --> 00:27:26.552
MAN: I don't know what to do with you!
WOMAN: He's just a boy!

316
00:27:26.640 --> 00:27:29.837
- I can't leave the room for 10 minutes!
- I didn't... Go away! Go to hell!

317
00:27:29.920 --> 00:27:31.876
- MAN: I'm sick of it!
- Let's go get lover-boy!

318
00:27:31.960 --> 00:27:33.837
I'm gonna kill you, kid!

319
00:27:33.920 --> 00:27:36.070
Not so fast, that's my kid.

320
00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:41.197
- Mad Dog Maguire?
- Ricochet O'Connell.

321
00:27:41.680 --> 00:27:44.069
- Hey, hey.
- EVELYN: What are you doing here?

322
00:27:44.160 --> 00:27:46.913
- Alex! Sweetheart! Are you all right?
- Just a little family get-together, folks.

323
00:27:47.000 --> 00:27:50.276
Come on,
let's get back to having a good time. Music!

324
00:27:50.760 --> 00:27:51.749
How long has it been?

325
00:27:51.840 --> 00:27:54.559
Egypt, '23. French Foreign Legion.

326
00:27:55.880 --> 00:27:57.757
This guy could land a plane
on anything, you...

327
00:27:57.840 --> 00:28:00.354
- Why are you here?
- Ricochet, he had his hands all over me girl.

328
00:28:00.440 --> 00:28:02.635
Now, son or no son,
I gotta give him a beating!

329
00:28:02.720 --> 00:28:04.950
- Get out of the way, Dad.
- Sit down.

330
00:28:05.040 --> 00:28:07.679
Now as much as I'd really like you
to teach him a valuable lesson...

331
00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:09.352
His mother would be upset! Very upset.

332
00:28:09.440 --> 00:28:10.919
You have a lot of explaining to do,
young man.

333
00:28:11.000 --> 00:28:12.149
I got a wife now, and a kid.

334
00:28:12.240 --> 00:28:14.310
Things are a little bit different,
I'm sure you understand.

335
00:28:14.400 --> 00:28:16.038
- Yeah.
- Let me make it up to you.

336
00:28:17.280 --> 00:28:19.316
We're just surprised to see you here.
That's all.

337
00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:20.753
JONATHAN: Who's gonna pay
for all this damage?

338
00:28:20.840 --> 00:28:22.068
All right?

339
00:28:22.160 --> 00:28:23.149
I'm not here five minutes,

340
00:28:23.240 --> 00:28:25.037
and I'm already pulling your fanny
out of the fire.

341
00:28:25.120 --> 00:28:26.109
You're going back to college.

342
00:28:26.200 --> 00:28:29.237
How'd you think this was gonna work, Dad?
You two show up, tell me what to do?

343
00:28:29.320 --> 00:28:33.598
No. But we should sit down
and discuss this like a family.

344
00:28:33.680 --> 00:28:36.353
No offence, Mom,
but we haven't been a family in a long time.

345
00:28:36.440 --> 00:28:38.396
Hey, don't you turn your back on me. Alex!

346
00:28:38.480 --> 00:28:40.710
Alex, just... Alex, come here.

347
00:28:42.640 --> 00:28:44.073
Can you...

348
00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:47.436
Don't look at me like that.

349
00:28:47.520 --> 00:28:48.509
(SIGHS)

350
00:28:53.080 --> 00:28:55.355
- It's all your fault!
- My fault?

351
00:28:55.440 --> 00:28:57.078
You're the one
that's always smothering him.

352
00:28:57.160 --> 00:28:59.594
You couldn't leave him alone
for five minutes without wiping his nose.

353
00:28:59.680 --> 00:29:03.275
Perhaps I was overcompensating for the fact
that you never took an interest in his life.

354
00:29:03.360 --> 00:29:05.920
His life was my top priority.

355
00:29:06.000 --> 00:29:08.468
How many times did I save that kid
from breaking his neck?

356
00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:10.710
A little warmth and encouragement
would have been nice.

357
00:29:10.800 --> 00:29:13.394
I'm his father. It's implied.

358
00:29:16.440 --> 00:29:20.115
We've spent our entire lives
searching for priceless artefacts,

359
00:29:20.200 --> 00:29:21.713
and the one thing
that's most precious to us,

360
00:29:21.800 --> 00:29:22.789
we've lost.

361
00:29:24.440 --> 00:29:29.230
We can't let Alex become some stranger
in pictures on our mantle.

362
00:29:29.960 --> 00:29:31.632
- We can't let that happen.
- No, we can't.

363
00:29:31.720 --> 00:29:33.756
How are we gonna fix this?

364
00:29:35.280 --> 00:29:37.396
We need to do it together.

365
00:29:43.640 --> 00:29:47.838
PARAMILITARY OUTPOST
WESTERN CHINA

366
00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:49.592
(MACHINE GUNS FIRING)

367
00:30:10.240 --> 00:30:11.309
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

368
00:30:11.400 --> 00:30:14.073
The O'Connells are in Shanghai.

369
00:30:14.640 --> 00:30:17.029
Do they have the Eye of Shangri-La?

370
00:30:17.120 --> 00:30:19.395
Our spy says they do.

371
00:30:19.880 --> 00:30:20.869
Good.

372
00:30:21.080 --> 00:30:22.195
Assemble the troops!

373
00:30:22.280 --> 00:30:23.269
Yes sir.

374
00:30:27.600 --> 00:30:28.589
Soldiers!

375
00:30:29.160 --> 00:30:32.436
Soon all our training and sacrifice...

376
00:30:33.080 --> 00:30:35.514
will bear great fruit.

377
00:30:36.520 --> 00:30:39.637
It is my dream to raise our Emperor
from his tomb.

378
00:30:40.320 --> 00:30:43.312
Only He can bring order out of this chaos.

379
00:30:44.320 --> 00:30:45.309
Soldiers...

380
00:30:46.480 --> 00:30:50.029
tonight our great battle begins!

381
00:30:50.120 --> 00:30:51.553
(ALL CHANTING)

382
00:30:52.600 --> 00:30:55.319
(PEOPLE CHEERING)

383
00:31:00.760 --> 00:31:04.116
You know, this might have been faster
if we took a rickshaw.

384
00:31:04.200 --> 00:31:06.430
It's Chinese New Year.

385
00:31:06.520 --> 00:31:07.509
Don't you just love this country?

386
00:31:07.600 --> 00:31:10.831
They have so many extra little holidays,
and drinking is mandatory.

387
00:31:10.920 --> 00:31:13.388
I can't believe
we get to see your first big discovery.

388
00:31:13.480 --> 00:31:14.469
It's so exciting.

389
00:31:14.560 --> 00:31:16.949
Well, after last night,
I'm surprised you want to see it at all.

390
00:31:18.360 --> 00:31:20.874
JONATHAN: Listen,
I'll pick you up in about an hour.

391
00:31:20.960 --> 00:31:22.188
EVELYN: You're not coming?

392
00:31:22.280 --> 00:31:25.477
JONATHAN: No, no,
I've seen enough mummies to last a lifetime.

393
00:31:36.320 --> 00:31:37.719
There he is.

394
00:31:38.320 --> 00:31:41.596
Oh, my darling, very impressive.

395
00:31:42.520 --> 00:31:44.158
When do you get to open the sarcophagus?

396
00:31:44.240 --> 00:31:46.196
ALEX: Well,
after the official red tape has been cut.

397
00:31:46.280 --> 00:31:49.431
Do the words "rest in peace"
mean anything to you two?

398
00:31:49.520 --> 00:31:53.069
So, Mom, why don't you stick around
for the next few days,

399
00:31:53.160 --> 00:31:54.354
and we can open it together?

400
00:31:54.440 --> 00:31:55.793
I would like that very much, thanks.

401
00:31:55.880 --> 00:31:58.075
Alex, why don't you go
and tell Professor Wilson

402
00:31:58.160 --> 00:32:00.151
that we're here. You know...

403
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:01.559
No problem. Great.

404
00:32:01.640 --> 00:32:04.677
Just don't wake the big guy up
while I'm gone.

405
00:32:11.160 --> 00:32:12.559
Hey, Alex.

406
00:32:13.160 --> 00:32:17.631
You know, this is all really, really big stuff.

407
00:32:20.920 --> 00:32:22.831
Whatever you say, Dad.

408
00:32:45.560 --> 00:32:48.313
(WHISTLING)

409
00:32:58.400 --> 00:32:59.594
What?

410
00:33:00.560 --> 00:33:05.395
You just have a certain glow about you
this evening I haven't seen in a long time.

411
00:33:06.840 --> 00:33:09.638
I guess mummies bring out the best in me.

412
00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:14.190
Take a wrong turn at Cairo?
Sorry to interrupt.

413
00:33:15.760 --> 00:33:17.637
- Roger.
- Professor Roger Wilson.

414
00:33:17.720 --> 00:33:18.994
Rick.

415
00:33:19.080 --> 00:33:22.470
You know, when Alex told me
that you had gone legit,

416
00:33:22.560 --> 00:33:24.516
I just couldn't believe my ears.

417
00:33:24.600 --> 00:33:28.149
Well, now I just pillage tombs
in the name of preservation. Evelyn.

418
00:33:28.240 --> 00:33:32.199
- Congratulations on your latest discovery.
- Alex deserves all the credit.

419
00:33:32.280 --> 00:33:34.271
He's one hell of a kid.
He's like the son I never had.

420
00:33:34.360 --> 00:33:35.634
And he's the only one we've got,

421
00:33:35.720 --> 00:33:37.676
so the next time you send him
on one of your field trips,

422
00:33:37.760 --> 00:33:38.988
you give us the heads-up first.

423
00:33:39.080 --> 00:33:41.355
Yes, yes, of course.

424
00:33:41.440 --> 00:33:44.716
And now, I believe you have
something that belongs to us.

425
00:33:44.800 --> 00:33:46.313
What's that?

426
00:33:46.400 --> 00:33:47.958
Oh, you mean this?

427
00:33:48.040 --> 00:33:49.029
(GASPS)

428
00:33:49.360 --> 00:33:51.396
(LAUGHING)

429
00:33:51.480 --> 00:33:52.913
I'm sorry...

430
00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:56.232
There, go ahead.

431
00:33:56.320 --> 00:33:58.038
All yours, Rog.

432
00:33:58.960 --> 00:34:01.428
I knew I could rely on you two.

433
00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:06.913
I'm afraid your work is not done yet,
Mr and Mrs O'Connell.

434
00:34:07.000 --> 00:34:10.754
I'd like to introduce you to a friend of mine.
General Yang.

435
00:34:10.840 --> 00:34:11.989
Roger!

436
00:34:12.440 --> 00:34:16.592
Well, he is the man who financed Alex's dig.
We're in this together.

437
00:34:17.440 --> 00:34:19.351
Cheek by jowl. General.

438
00:34:21.280 --> 00:34:22.713
Search him.

439
00:34:24.560 --> 00:34:28.519
No. The Eye belongs to the Chinese people.
You can't do this.

440
00:34:28.600 --> 00:34:32.912
So, Rog, you snake, how much did...

441
00:34:33.000 --> 00:34:35.673
Is it Yin and Yang? ...pay you?

442
00:34:35.760 --> 00:34:38.194
Enough to pull strings at the Foreign Office,

443
00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:42.512
make sure that it was you two
who delivered the Eye. Turn around.

444
00:34:42.600 --> 00:34:46.434
The Eye contains the elixir
from the Pool of Eternal Life.

445
00:34:48.440 --> 00:34:51.113
I need you to open it, Mrs O'Connell.

446
00:34:52.320 --> 00:34:53.469
No.

447
00:34:54.200 --> 00:34:56.430
You're going to use it to wake the Emperor,
aren't you?

448
00:34:56.520 --> 00:35:00.513
And his Terracotta Army.
At least, that's the general idea.

449
00:35:00.600 --> 00:35:03.990
Raising an army of mummies is insane.
Listen, Yang...

450
00:35:05.560 --> 00:35:07.471
(GRUNTING)

451
00:35:07.560 --> 00:35:09.232
Easy! Go easy.

452
00:35:10.040 --> 00:35:13.032
Time to open the sarcophagus. Move!

453
00:35:17.400 --> 00:35:20.597
Read the inscription! Now!

454
00:35:28.360 --> 00:35:30.954
Ancient Chinese isn't my forte.

455
00:35:31.040 --> 00:35:34.430
Here's some encouragement. Wilson!

456
00:35:35.560 --> 00:35:36.549
I'll do it!

457
00:35:36.640 --> 00:35:40.189
No, Evy, don't do it!
They're just gonna kill me, anyway.

458
00:35:44.040 --> 00:35:46.679
The inscription says
that only a drop of blood

459
00:35:46.760 --> 00:35:49.832
from a person of pure heart
can open the Eye.

460
00:35:51.800 --> 00:35:53.711
Your husband was right.

461
00:35:55.480 --> 00:35:56.959
No!

462
00:36:03.480 --> 00:36:07.837
Only the pure of heart would sacrifice
themselves for the one they love.

463
00:36:09.120 --> 00:36:10.599
Open it.

464
00:36:15.360 --> 00:36:18.158
You never called after our last date.

465
00:36:18.240 --> 00:36:20.470
I don't have time for games, Alex.

466
00:36:20.560 --> 00:36:23.791
You know my name, but I don't know yours.

467
00:36:23.880 --> 00:36:25.029
It's Lin.

468
00:36:25.120 --> 00:36:28.510
You want to explain to me
why you tried to kill me?

469
00:36:28.600 --> 00:36:29.669
We could do that.

470
00:36:29.760 --> 00:36:31.478
Or we could save your parents.

471
00:36:36.280 --> 00:36:38.840
Wilson, you son of a bitch!

472
00:36:52.320 --> 00:36:54.072
(GRUNTING)

473
00:37:29.000 --> 00:37:32.231
- Get on with it, O'Connell.
- All right.

474
00:37:46.080 --> 00:37:47.069
(COUGHS)

475
00:37:50.440 --> 00:37:55.753
Once this touches him,
the Emperor will rise to rule again.

476
00:37:56.800 --> 00:37:57.789
Finish him off.

477
00:37:57.880 --> 00:37:58.869
(GUN COCKING)

478
00:38:15.640 --> 00:38:18.074
(GRUNTING)

479
00:38:35.760 --> 00:38:38.035
Alex, please! Don't. That's...

480
00:38:38.600 --> 00:38:40.750
Don't, don't. Don't, please.

481
00:38:40.840 --> 00:38:43.400
No, don't, Alex, it's me. Please.

482
00:38:43.840 --> 00:38:47.435
It's not him. This is a eunuch! It's a decoy!

483
00:38:49.360 --> 00:38:51.316
Where the hell's the Emperor?

484
00:38:52.480 --> 00:38:55.074
(CLANGING)

485
00:39:16.560 --> 00:39:17.754
Stay!

486
00:39:31.040 --> 00:39:33.395
(BREATHES DEEPLY)

487
00:39:35.840 --> 00:39:37.432
Here we go again.

488
00:39:48.160 --> 00:39:49.149
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

489
00:39:49.240 --> 00:39:51.037
I live to serve you, my Lord.

490
00:39:51.120 --> 00:39:52.633
I can help you become immortal.

491
00:39:52.720 --> 00:39:55.439
If you are lying, you will burn.

492
00:40:11.360 --> 00:40:15.433
Wait! Wait! You wait for me!
I'm coming with you! Wait, wait...

493
00:40:27.360 --> 00:40:30.432
(BOTH GRUNTING)

494
00:40:40.280 --> 00:40:41.599
Watch out!

495
00:40:46.680 --> 00:40:50.434
RICK: We got to put this mummy down fast!
The longer we wait, the stronger they get!

496
00:40:50.520 --> 00:40:52.750
Open the gate! Open the gate!

497
00:40:57.880 --> 00:40:59.711
(SHOUTING IN MANDARIN)

498
00:40:59.800 --> 00:41:03.475
Yeah, yeah, yeah, I know. Sorry, pal.
There's a mummy on the loose.

499
00:41:03.560 --> 00:41:04.788
- You wanna drive?
- Why not?

500
00:41:04.880 --> 00:41:06.598
God, I love a woman who can drive a truck.

501
00:41:06.680 --> 00:41:09.638
Hey, pal, I'm really sorry,
but you know what? Happy New Year!

502
00:41:09.960 --> 00:41:11.188
Hit it, honey!

503
00:41:16.320 --> 00:41:17.958
No! Move over!

504
00:41:19.200 --> 00:41:20.792
What? No!

505
00:41:20.880 --> 00:41:22.154
No!

506
00:41:25.120 --> 00:41:26.109
(SCREAMS)

507
00:41:28.960 --> 00:41:30.234
No!

508
00:41:31.720 --> 00:41:34.154
- What?
- Jonathan, get in the back!

509
00:41:35.440 --> 00:41:36.509
Sorry about the Rolls!

510
00:41:36.600 --> 00:41:38.909
You guys are like mummy magnets!

511
00:41:40.520 --> 00:41:42.988
- We have to turn you around!
- Okay.

512
00:41:48.640 --> 00:41:49.993
Excuse me.

513
00:41:52.360 --> 00:41:54.954
- Hey, we could use this!
- Give me that!

514
00:41:57.200 --> 00:42:00.476
- Oh, yeah, that's a better idea.
- RICK: Size counts!

515
00:42:00.560 --> 00:42:03.358
Stop mucking about! They're getting away!

516
00:42:04.240 --> 00:42:05.912
(GRUNTS) Just drive!

517
00:42:06.560 --> 00:42:08.676
RICK: Aim for the Emperor!
JONATHAN: Aim for the Emperor?

518
00:42:08.760 --> 00:42:11.320
- Light it up, Jonathan!
- I'm trying!

519
00:42:11.400 --> 00:42:12.469
Fire!

520
00:42:12.560 --> 00:42:13.549
(SCREAMS)

521
00:42:23.200 --> 00:42:25.031
(PEOPLE SCREAMING)

522
00:42:32.280 --> 00:42:33.713
Did we get him?

523
00:42:33.800 --> 00:42:35.836
- Fire!
- What, again?

524
00:42:35.920 --> 00:42:37.751
- Your ass is on fire!
- My ass?

525
00:42:37.840 --> 00:42:39.637
- Hold still!
- Rick, my ass is on fire!

526
00:42:39.720 --> 00:42:41.119
- Well, spank my...
- I'm putting it out!

527
00:42:41.200 --> 00:42:42.872
- Put me out, Rick!
- Just hold still!

528
00:42:42.960 --> 00:42:45.155
Spank my ass! Spank my ass!

529
00:42:45.240 --> 00:42:47.117
All right, here I come!

530
00:42:49.960 --> 00:42:51.678
LIN: Give me your hand!

531
00:42:57.640 --> 00:42:58.629
Come on!

532
00:42:59.200 --> 00:43:00.553
Watch out!

533
00:43:01.440 --> 00:43:02.509
RICK: Evy, where are you going?

534
00:43:02.600 --> 00:43:04.636
- Taking a short cut!
- Evy!

535
00:43:05.000 --> 00:43:07.036
(BOTH SCREAMING)

536
00:43:13.720 --> 00:43:15.676
- I told you it was a short cut!
- Right!

537
00:43:15.760 --> 00:43:17.557
Now he's chasing us!

538
00:43:18.560 --> 00:43:19.549
(YELPS)

539
00:43:20.800 --> 00:43:21.789
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

540
00:43:21.880 --> 00:43:23.074
Hurry!

541
00:43:24.200 --> 00:43:26.760
Give me your hand.
Here, you're gonna need these.

542
00:43:26.840 --> 00:43:28.637
- Don't wait up for me.
- Where are you going?

543
00:43:28.720 --> 00:43:29.789
Out!

544
00:43:35.680 --> 00:43:38.240
- Where's Rick?
- Where do you think?

545
00:43:44.200 --> 00:43:45.519
Damn it!

546
00:43:49.480 --> 00:43:50.913
You're mine!

547
00:43:51.000 --> 00:43:53.230
(HORSES NEIGHING)

548
00:43:55.880 --> 00:43:59.350
- Give me your hand and get on this horse!
- Get back, Dad!

549
00:43:59.440 --> 00:44:04.195
Alexander Rupert O'Connell, you get
on the back of this horse this instant!

550
00:44:10.440 --> 00:44:13.113
(EXCLAIMING)

551
00:44:13.200 --> 00:44:17.193
Get out of the way! Get out of the way!
Oh, God!

552
00:44:23.040 --> 00:44:24.075
(SCREAMING)

553
00:44:24.160 --> 00:44:25.275
JONATHAN: Evy!

554
00:44:26.320 --> 00:44:27.833
We've got to go back and help Rick!

555
00:44:27.920 --> 00:44:30.673
JONATHAN: Rick! Forget Rick!
Here they come!

556
00:44:38.880 --> 00:44:40.472
I'll go after the Emperor.

557
00:44:40.560 --> 00:44:43.199
Trust me. I've got a little more experience
with mummies.

558
00:44:43.280 --> 00:44:46.636
And I have the only weapon
that can kill him.

559
00:44:46.720 --> 00:44:49.029
Okay. I'll cover you. Let's go!

560
00:44:57.040 --> 00:44:58.155
ALEX: Lin!

561
00:44:59.600 --> 00:45:00.589
(SCREAMS)

562
00:45:15.160 --> 00:45:17.754
- I thought you were dead!
- He missed.

563
00:45:29.040 --> 00:45:32.191
(EXCLAIMING)

564
00:45:43.640 --> 00:45:44.993
LIN: Look out!

565
00:46:24.520 --> 00:46:26.988
(PANTING)

566
00:46:29.360 --> 00:46:33.717
- Thanks, Rick. Could you get the cab?
- Does it look like I have a wallet?

567
00:46:51.960 --> 00:46:54.599
You know, I would have killed the Emperor
if you two hadn't blown my cover.

568
00:46:54.680 --> 00:46:55.874
I had everything under control.

569
00:46:55.960 --> 00:46:58.110
Oh, yeah, that's exactly
what we were thinking.

570
00:46:58.200 --> 00:46:59.952
Yeah, well, good going,
you raised another mummy.

571
00:47:00.040 --> 00:47:01.917
And this bugger's got superpowers.

572
00:47:02.000 --> 00:47:05.117
ALEX: He's got control over fire, water,
metal and who knows what else.

573
00:47:05.200 --> 00:47:06.235
And you dug him up anyway.

574
00:47:06.320 --> 00:47:07.992
Yeah, well, you're not gonna
pin this one on me, okay, Dad?

575
00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:10.230
- RICK: Am I?
- Oh, stop it, you two.

576
00:47:10.320 --> 00:47:13.596
No one's to blame here.
Wilson manipulated all of us.

577
00:47:13.680 --> 00:47:14.749
Yeah, that's true.

578
00:47:14.840 --> 00:47:16.831
I apologise for my parents.

579
00:47:16.920 --> 00:47:19.639
But I thought we worked
really well together.

580
00:47:20.120 --> 00:47:21.792
Except we failed.

581
00:47:23.920 --> 00:47:27.071
I'm sorry,
we haven't been properly introduced.

582
00:47:27.160 --> 00:47:29.628
- Who are you exactly?
- My name is Lin.

583
00:47:29.720 --> 00:47:32.951
My family has watched
over the Emperor's tomb for centuries.

584
00:47:33.040 --> 00:47:37.192
The Emperor cannot be killed unless
he is stabbed through the heart with this.

585
00:47:37.280 --> 00:47:39.874
My mother put a curse on it long ago.

586
00:47:41.200 --> 00:47:42.189
Mmm-hmm.

587
00:47:43.120 --> 00:47:45.634
Well, a quick family meeting, Alex.

588
00:47:47.320 --> 00:47:48.799
- Sit.
- Down.

589
00:47:50.760 --> 00:47:52.671
What do you really know about this girl?

590
00:47:52.760 --> 00:47:57.311
Well, not much, but after her help tonight,
I'm willing to go on a little faith.

591
00:47:57.400 --> 00:47:59.197
- Faith.
- Time is running out.

592
00:47:59.280 --> 00:48:01.669
You don't really believe in the concept
of personal space, do you?

593
00:48:01.760 --> 00:48:05.116
If the Emperor reaches Shangri-La
and drinks from the Pool of Eternal Life,

594
00:48:05.200 --> 00:48:07.953
he will raise his army
and no one will be safe.

595
00:48:08.040 --> 00:48:10.474
Much as I'd like to stay
this boyishly handsome forever,

596
00:48:10.560 --> 00:48:11.959
Shangri-La is a crock.

597
00:48:12.040 --> 00:48:13.917
Yeah, but that's what you used to say
about mummies, too, Jon.

598
00:48:14.000 --> 00:48:16.036
- You did pretty well off it.
- Good point.

599
00:48:16.120 --> 00:48:20.352
The Gateway to Shangri-La lies in
a mountain pass high in the Himalayas.

600
00:48:20.440 --> 00:48:22.510
Beyond it is a golden tower.

601
00:48:22.600 --> 00:48:26.149
Once the diamond is placed at the top,
it will point the way to Shangri-La.

602
00:48:26.240 --> 00:48:28.196
Yang still has the diamond,

603
00:48:28.280 --> 00:48:31.158
and that's where
he and the Emperor will go.

604
00:48:31.680 --> 00:48:32.669
She's right.

605
00:48:32.760 --> 00:48:35.718
All the legends of the Eye
mention the Gateway.

606
00:48:35.800 --> 00:48:37.870
I like her, Alex. She knows what's what.

607
00:48:37.960 --> 00:48:43.239
Now, just say that we were to believe you,
could you guide us there?

608
00:48:43.320 --> 00:48:46.596
Yes. I have been there once.
I remember the way.

609
00:48:49.320 --> 00:48:51.675
Himalayas. We're going to need a plane.

610
00:48:51.760 --> 00:48:54.433
Well, I know just the Mad Dog for the job.

611
00:48:57.680 --> 00:49:00.478
MAGUIRE: Well, any self-respecting pilot
would land on the valley floor,

612
00:49:00.560 --> 00:49:02.232
but I don't have any self-respect,

613
00:49:02.320 --> 00:49:04.470
so I'll put you down
halfway up the mountain.

614
00:49:04.560 --> 00:49:06.232
That should give us a good advantage.

615
00:49:06.320 --> 00:49:08.311
MAGUIRE: Of course,
I can't guarantee any of us will live.

616
00:49:08.400 --> 00:49:09.549
Great!

617
00:49:13.160 --> 00:49:16.869
I'd tell you to fasten your seatbelts,
but I was too cheap to buy any!

618
00:49:16.960 --> 00:49:19.076
(LAUGHING)

619
00:49:19.560 --> 00:49:21.835
- Why am I laughing?
- Here we go!

620
00:49:22.760 --> 00:49:25.877
RICK: Mad Dog, Mad Dog!
Ease up, ease up, ease up!

621
00:49:26.240 --> 00:49:27.639
JONATHAN: Oh, God!

622
00:49:30.120 --> 00:49:32.554
(SCREAMING)

623
00:49:35.080 --> 00:49:36.752
JONATHAN: Maguire!

624
00:49:38.360 --> 00:49:39.873
Come on, man!

625
00:49:40.320 --> 00:49:41.514
Mad Dog!

626
00:49:48.800 --> 00:49:50.438
(YAK BELLOWING)

627
00:49:53.480 --> 00:49:55.072
RICK: Brake! No, no! Nobody move.

628
00:49:55.160 --> 00:49:57.799
Nobody move, nobody move!

629
00:50:10.680 --> 00:50:12.830
What is that God-awful smell?

630
00:50:14.120 --> 00:50:15.712
The yak yakked.

631
00:50:18.880 --> 00:50:19.869
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

632
00:50:19.960 --> 00:50:22.190
Welcome to the modern world, my Lord.

633
00:50:22.720 --> 00:50:24.551
Why did you raise me?

634
00:50:24.960 --> 00:50:28.999
I love this land.
Only you can lead us back to greatness.

635
00:50:29.840 --> 00:50:32.115
What is in it for you?

636
00:50:33.640 --> 00:50:36.313
I want to serve as your general.

637
00:50:37.000 --> 00:50:39.355
The last general I trusted...

638
00:50:39.640 --> 00:50:42.313
betrayed me.

639
00:50:42.880 --> 00:50:45.519
I will not make that mistake.

640
00:50:51.680 --> 00:50:56.037
I cannot escape this curse
until I am immortal...

641
00:50:56.800 --> 00:50:58.233
General.

642
00:50:59.880 --> 00:51:01.791
I understand, my Lord.

643
00:51:02.080 --> 00:51:05.789
We need to find the Pool of Eternal Life.

644
00:51:06.640 --> 00:51:10.349
This will point the way.

645
00:51:12.440 --> 00:51:15.238
(ROARS)

646
00:51:30.920 --> 00:51:32.592
(MAGUIRE SINGING)
<i>Can't you see it's Mr McGuire</i>

647
00:51:32.680 --> 00:51:34.432
<i>come to court your sister Kate</i>

648
00:51:34.520 --> 00:51:38.433
<i>You know very well he owns the farm</i>
<i>a wee bit out...</i>

649
00:51:38.520 --> 00:51:40.272
(PLANE ENGINE HUMMING)

650
00:51:50.280 --> 00:51:53.317
<i>MAGUIRE OVER RADIO: Delta-Tango-Alpha</i>
<i>to Ricochet. Come in, Ricochet.</i>

651
00:51:55.240 --> 00:51:57.629
Delta-Tango-Alpha, this is Ricochet.
Go ahead, Mad Dog.

652
00:51:57.720 --> 00:52:00.075
Yeah, you know that Yang fellow
you told me to keep me eye out for?

653
00:52:00.160 --> 00:52:01.309
<i>He's just shown up.</i>

654
00:52:01.400 --> 00:52:03.550
Ricochet out. Thanks, Mad Dog.

655
00:52:03.640 --> 00:52:05.232
That's us, people! Let's go!

656
00:52:05.320 --> 00:52:07.072
- Jonathan, wake up!
- What...

657
00:52:16.440 --> 00:52:17.953
Hold the line!

658
00:52:21.320 --> 00:52:22.435
Good, we're a little more than halfway.

659
00:52:22.520 --> 00:52:25.910
We're gonna...
We're gonna camp up there for the night.

660
00:52:38.160 --> 00:52:42.233
ALEX: Lin says if we leave at first light,
we'll reach the Gateway by noon.

661
00:52:43.720 --> 00:52:47.508
Did she happen to mention how she knows
so much about the Gateway?

662
00:52:47.600 --> 00:52:50.273
No, not really. Kind of mysterious.

663
00:52:51.040 --> 00:52:53.679
She's certainly managed to enchant you.

664
00:52:55.760 --> 00:52:58.320
Come on, Alex. You obviously like her.

665
00:53:00.160 --> 00:53:03.630
Mom, the thin mountain air,
clearly messing with your head.

666
00:53:05.440 --> 00:53:07.556
Whatever secret she's hiding,

667
00:53:08.760 --> 00:53:10.796
I just don't want to see you get hurt.

668
00:53:10.880 --> 00:53:14.190
I appreciate that, but, you know,

669
00:53:14.280 --> 00:53:18.159
I've had my fair share of experience
with the opposite sex.

670
00:53:18.240 --> 00:53:19.355
Really?

671
00:53:21.040 --> 00:53:23.713
How many experiences
are we talking about?

672
00:53:24.960 --> 00:53:29.954
Well, you shouldn't ask questions you don't
want to know the answer to, okay, Mom?

673
00:53:30.040 --> 00:53:31.109
Right.

674
00:53:32.200 --> 00:53:33.997
Hey, Mom.

675
00:53:35.920 --> 00:53:39.390
I'm sorry I blamed you guys
for raising the Emperor.

676
00:53:50.120 --> 00:53:51.712
What's so funny?

677
00:53:54.800 --> 00:53:58.998
My mother is under the impression
there's something between us.

678
00:53:59.080 --> 00:54:00.991
I hope nothing romantic.

679
00:54:03.880 --> 00:54:07.316
Yeah, well, I told her there
was no chance of that.

680
00:54:07.400 --> 00:54:09.675
We're complete opposites,
you and me, right?

681
00:54:09.760 --> 00:54:14.595
You guard tombs. I raid them.
You like ancient knives. I'm into guns.

682
00:54:15.280 --> 00:54:17.635
Those are some
pretty insurmountable odds.

683
00:54:17.720 --> 00:54:19.870
- Absolutely.
- Well, good.

684
00:54:20.720 --> 00:54:24.759
Now that we've cleared that up,
we can focus on taking down the Emperor.

685
00:54:24.840 --> 00:54:26.398
I agree totally.

686
00:54:28.920 --> 00:54:31.514
Besides, you're not my type.

687
00:54:34.360 --> 00:54:38.319
Of course not. You don't like a woman
who can knock you on your backside.

688
00:54:38.400 --> 00:54:40.436
(CHUCKLES)

689
00:54:40.520 --> 00:54:42.829
The expression is "kick my ass."

690
00:54:43.800 --> 00:54:46.189
And for the record, you didn't.

691
00:54:48.800 --> 00:54:51.917
Yeah, it's not easy being me, you know.

692
00:54:52.000 --> 00:54:53.638
Then again, I don't suppose
it's easy being you,

693
00:54:53.720 --> 00:54:55.790
is it, Geraldine, old girl?

694
00:54:55.880 --> 00:54:57.996
If I'd met a girl like you, Geraldine...

695
00:54:58.080 --> 00:55:00.878
You know, hard-working,
you don't say much,

696
00:55:01.880 --> 00:55:05.156
you're a little bit hairy, but I don't mind that.

697
00:55:15.800 --> 00:55:17.950
There it is! We found it!

698
00:55:25.600 --> 00:55:27.556
The Gateway of Shangri-La!

699
00:55:34.760 --> 00:55:38.548
JONATHAN: Go, girl! Go! You're free!

700
00:55:38.640 --> 00:55:41.712
Go, Geraldine! Live free!

701
00:55:51.480 --> 00:55:54.074
What did you do now? Rob an armoury?

702
00:55:55.200 --> 00:55:57.475
Have you ever seen a Walther P38?

703
00:55:57.560 --> 00:55:59.710
Looks pretty anaemic
compared to the Peacekeeper.

704
00:55:59.800 --> 00:56:03.031
Well, it's not about size, Dad.
It's about stamina.

705
00:56:05.440 --> 00:56:06.919
You want power?

706
00:56:08.240 --> 00:56:13.155
I give you the Thompson submachine gun.
Fifty rounds a drum.

707
00:56:13.240 --> 00:56:16.277
- Twenty-five a mag.
- Tommy's good, Dad,

708
00:56:16.360 --> 00:56:17.998
but the cocking mechanism always jams.

709
00:56:18.080 --> 00:56:22.278
Here. Check out the Russian PPS
Personal Assault Weapon.

710
00:56:22.360 --> 00:56:23.998
Now, this is the future right here.

711
00:56:24.080 --> 00:56:27.311
You know, it's experience that wins the day.
It's not all about firepower.

712
00:56:27.400 --> 00:56:29.277
Boys! If I may...

713
00:56:29.360 --> 00:56:31.157
Do we have a plan for the Emperor?

714
00:56:31.240 --> 00:56:33.117
Yeah. We're gonna hit him
high, hard and fast

715
00:56:33.200 --> 00:56:34.872
and smash him like a Ming vase.

716
00:56:34.960 --> 00:56:37.952
- And if that doesn't work?
- We go to plan B.

717
00:56:38.040 --> 00:56:41.077
Plan B! You go upstairs,
you blow up that gold tower thing.

718
00:56:41.160 --> 00:56:43.196
- You light it up. We blow the guy sky high!
- Me?

719
00:56:43.280 --> 00:56:44.269
- You! What?
- Dad?

720
00:56:44.360 --> 00:56:46.396
So if the explosion doesn't kill us,
the avalanche will.

721
00:56:46.480 --> 00:56:47.913
- You got a better idea?
- Yeah. I do.

722
00:56:48.000 --> 00:56:49.797
I say we ambush him
with long-range rifles and silencers.

723
00:56:49.880 --> 00:56:50.915
Long-range, that's a better idea.

724
00:56:51.000 --> 00:56:52.035
Yeah, we can get in close, Dad.

725
00:56:52.120 --> 00:56:53.189
- JONATHAN: Much better idea.
- And then we can finish him off

726
00:56:53.280 --> 00:56:54.838
- with Lin's dagger.
- Look, I'm sorry,

727
00:56:54.920 --> 00:56:57.480
I just don't put much faith
in your girlfriend's magic dagger.

728
00:56:57.560 --> 00:56:59.676
- Okay, Dad, she is not my girlfriend.
- You say that now,

729
00:56:59.760 --> 00:57:01.751
- but I still don't trust her.
- Well, I do.

730
00:57:01.840 --> 00:57:04.434
- So you should trust my judgement, okay?
- Look, kid,

731
00:57:04.520 --> 00:57:06.112
I've put down more mummies
in my time than you.

732
00:57:06.200 --> 00:57:07.553
You put down one mummy, Dad.

733
00:57:07.640 --> 00:57:10.712
Yeah. Same mummy twice!

734
00:57:15.040 --> 00:57:17.679
EVELYN: Hand me the green wire,
will you, please?

735
00:57:18.680 --> 00:57:20.511
Are you sure you know what you are doing?

736
00:57:20.600 --> 00:57:22.670
Of course. I've done this a hundred times.

737
00:57:22.760 --> 00:57:26.196
If the Emperor places the Eye up there,
all will be lost.

738
00:57:30.520 --> 00:57:32.397
(PANTING)

739
00:57:38.400 --> 00:57:39.389
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

740
00:57:39.480 --> 00:57:41.152
Clear a path to the Golden Tower.

741
00:57:41.680 --> 00:57:44.558
Prove yourself to me.

742
00:57:50.600 --> 00:57:51.589
(ORDERING TROOPS)

743
00:57:58.160 --> 00:57:59.878
Let's give a warm O'Connell welcome!

744
00:58:01.600 --> 00:58:03.113
(COMMANDING)

745
00:58:04.000 --> 00:58:05.115
Fire!

746
00:58:05.280 --> 00:58:06.872
(MACHINE GUN FIRING)

747
00:58:08.800 --> 00:58:11.439
(SCREAMING)

748
00:58:17.680 --> 00:58:18.908
Bazooka!

749
00:58:23.880 --> 00:58:25.199
RICK: Fall back!

750
00:58:34.200 --> 00:58:36.475
Alex! Follow me!

751
00:58:47.360 --> 00:58:49.351
(ORDERING IN MANDARIN)

752
00:58:51.200 --> 00:58:52.872
We gotta take out those bazookas!

753
00:58:54.840 --> 00:58:55.989
Go!

754
00:59:03.720 --> 00:59:05.039
Fall back!

755
00:59:05.560 --> 00:59:07.551
Move! Move! Move! Move!

756
00:59:14.760 --> 00:59:17.115
Time to go to plan B! Blow up the tower!

757
00:59:17.200 --> 00:59:18.997
Hey, I'm actually a little bit concerned
about plan B!

758
00:59:19.080 --> 00:59:20.433
Couldn't we go straight to plan C?

759
00:59:20.520 --> 00:59:23.034
Just make it go bang! I'll cover you!

760
00:59:24.160 --> 00:59:25.388
Come on.

761
00:59:26.200 --> 00:59:28.350
All right, let's go, go, go!
Come on, come on!

762
00:59:28.440 --> 00:59:30.192
Come on. Oh, be good.

763
00:59:48.120 --> 00:59:49.109
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

764
00:59:49.200 --> 00:59:50.679
Set up a crossfire!

765
00:59:51.320 --> 00:59:52.514
Move it!

766
00:59:56.616 --> 00:59:57.935
(GUN CLICKING)

767
01:00:01.056 --> 01:00:02.694
EVELYN: My last round!

768
01:00:06.736 --> 01:00:10.854
(SHOUTING IN FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

769
01:00:25.416 --> 01:00:29.409
- Abominable snowmen?
- The Tibetans call them yeti!

770
01:00:30.736 --> 01:00:31.851
(SNARLS)

771
01:00:32.296 --> 01:00:33.285
(SPEAKING FOREIGN LANGUAGE)

772
01:00:33.376 --> 01:00:34.729
Please! I need your help!

773
01:00:34.976 --> 01:00:36.932
These soldiers are evil!

774
01:00:39.016 --> 01:00:40.688
She speaks Yeti?

775
01:00:49.016 --> 01:00:50.688
(YETI ROARS)

776
01:00:55.496 --> 01:00:56.531
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

777
01:00:56.616 --> 01:00:58.208
Shoot! Kill them!

778
01:01:05.736 --> 01:01:08.409
Why do I always have to save the day?

779
01:01:09.016 --> 01:01:10.290
I hate it when the kid's right!

780
01:01:10.736 --> 01:01:12.613
(GRUNTING)

781
01:01:14.376 --> 01:01:15.968
Get the other guy!

782
01:01:16.896 --> 01:01:18.045
Thanks!

783
01:01:42.376 --> 01:01:43.604
Trouble!

784
01:01:53.896 --> 01:01:56.091
(SCREAMING)

785
01:01:59.056 --> 01:02:01.809
(ROARING)

786
01:02:05.536 --> 01:02:08.926
(GRUNTING)

787
01:02:21.536 --> 01:02:24.004
You can die slow or you can die fast.

788
01:02:30.536 --> 01:02:31.969
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

789
01:02:36.656 --> 01:02:38.453
(GRUNTING)

790
01:02:45.176 --> 01:02:47.451
Yes! Yes! Yes!

791
01:02:48.736 --> 01:02:51.125
(LAUGHING TRIUMPHANTLY)
Yeah! I did it!

792
01:02:51.776 --> 01:02:55.928
Oh, Mother, I did it!
Time for a retreat, I think.

793
01:03:00.936 --> 01:03:05.726
I'm on your team! I'm a team player!
"One for all and all for me" kind of thing!

794
01:03:06.656 --> 01:03:10.046
The dynamite, all this dynamite!
We should get out of here!

795
01:03:25.216 --> 01:03:26.649
Back off! Back off!

796
01:03:26.976 --> 01:03:28.489
LIN: Run!

797
01:03:37.376 --> 01:03:39.207
(ROARING)

798
01:03:55.136 --> 01:03:58.606
(GROANS) I hate mummies!
They never play fair!

799
01:04:06.336 --> 01:04:08.611
Dad! Dad, what are you doing?

800
01:04:15.976 --> 01:04:19.412
Over here! Over here! Come on! Over here!

801
01:04:20.176 --> 01:04:21.495
Oh, no!

802
01:04:26.896 --> 01:04:27.931
Rick!

803
01:04:30.776 --> 01:04:32.607
(SCREAMING)

804
01:04:54.136 --> 01:04:55.125
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

805
01:04:55.216 --> 01:04:57.093
Shangri-La.

806
01:05:05.456 --> 01:05:07.094
That's a diamond.

807
01:05:09.496 --> 01:05:10.975
I could use a diamond like that.

808
01:05:32.776 --> 01:05:34.004
Dad!

809
01:05:37.376 --> 01:05:38.695
(JONATHAN SCREAMS)

810
01:05:40.656 --> 01:05:43.090
Okay, hold it. Hold on there, Dad.

811
01:05:43.176 --> 01:05:46.168
All right, please, please, please
put pressure on it, okay, Dad?

812
01:05:46.256 --> 01:05:49.453
RICK: It's all right, it's all right.
We've been in tougher scrapes than this.

813
01:05:55.736 --> 01:05:57.294
Avalanche!

814
01:06:04.816 --> 01:06:07.888
(EMPEROR ROARING)

815
01:06:20.736 --> 01:06:21.725
(LIN GASPS)

816
01:06:28.536 --> 01:06:30.606
- Help! Help me!
- Lin!

817
01:06:35.496 --> 01:06:36.929
Please! Help me!

818
01:06:46.656 --> 01:06:48.692
(SCREAMING)

819
01:07:07.896 --> 01:07:09.295
(CRUNCHING)

820
01:07:11.696 --> 01:07:14.574
(YETI GROWLING)

821
01:07:16.936 --> 01:07:18.255
Yes!

822
01:07:18.336 --> 01:07:19.451
(LAUGHING HYSTERICALLY)

823
01:07:19.536 --> 01:07:21.970
I've got it! And I'm still alive!

824
01:07:25.696 --> 01:07:28.130
ALEX: (MUFFLED) Help me, please.
Somebody help me!

825
01:07:28.856 --> 01:07:31.575
- We're over here! Over here!
- Alex?

826
01:07:31.656 --> 01:07:34.124
- ALEX: Mom, Mom, we're down here!
- Alex?

827
01:07:34.456 --> 01:07:35.855
We're over here!

828
01:07:35.936 --> 01:07:37.608
(ALEX PANTING)

829
01:07:47.736 --> 01:07:48.964
Oh, God.

830
01:07:50.336 --> 01:07:54.045
We've got to take him to Shangri-La now!
It's our only chance.

831
01:08:12.816 --> 01:08:14.135
We made it!

832
01:08:31.296 --> 01:08:32.649
The Pool.

833
01:08:42.176 --> 01:08:43.211
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

834
01:08:43.296 --> 01:08:44.411
Mother.

835
01:08:45.856 --> 01:08:46.845
My sweet daughter.

836
01:08:55.376 --> 01:08:56.411
I beg you...

837
01:08:58.096 --> 01:08:59.893
My father is dying.

838
01:09:00.336 --> 01:09:01.564
They are my friends.

839
01:09:02.536 --> 01:09:03.855
Oh, please.

840
01:09:04.216 --> 01:09:05.205
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

841
01:09:21.456 --> 01:09:22.730
(RICK GASPS)

842
01:09:38.696 --> 01:09:40.015
Thank you.

843
01:09:41.376 --> 01:09:44.288
He must rest. We'll take him to my chamber.

844
01:10:00.456 --> 01:10:01.445
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

845
01:10:01.536 --> 01:10:04.926
Where are you going, General?
Our destiny awaits.

846
01:10:09.896 --> 01:10:14.412
Well, it's not everyone that gets
their brother-in-law back from the dead.

847
01:10:15.016 --> 01:10:18.213
Yeah, give me my four score years
and ten any day.

848
01:10:23.016 --> 01:10:24.813
Is this Shangri-La?

849
01:10:34.376 --> 01:10:37.095
I could live here. Lots of opportunity.

850
01:10:39.016 --> 01:10:40.415
A casino.

851
01:10:44.056 --> 01:10:45.045
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

852
01:10:45.136 --> 01:10:48.333
I was wrong to involve you in my revenge.

853
01:10:48.856 --> 01:10:50.289
No, mother.

854
01:10:51.336 --> 01:10:53.406
I would do anything for you.

855
01:11:02.336 --> 01:11:04.611
ALEX: He's resting well. Thank you.

856
01:11:06.296 --> 01:11:08.605
How'd you get involved in all this?

857
01:11:08.696 --> 01:11:13.531
The Emperor murdered the only man
I ever loved, Lin's father.

858
01:11:14.976 --> 01:11:17.695
I would have died, too, by his hand,

859
01:11:17.776 --> 01:11:21.530
if the yeti had not found me
and brought me to this pool.

860
01:11:21.616 --> 01:11:24.574
Hang on a second.
How did this all happen?

861
01:11:24.656 --> 01:11:26.533
This was before Christ.

862
01:11:29.376 --> 01:11:32.049
How long were you guarding his tomb?

863
01:11:32.136 --> 01:11:33.728
Over 2,000 years.

864
01:11:39.656 --> 01:11:41.851
The Emperor must never be
allowed to reach the Pool,

865
01:11:41.936 --> 01:11:44.734
or he will have the power to raise his army.

866
01:11:44.816 --> 01:11:46.374
And once he becomes immortal,

867
01:11:46.456 --> 01:11:50.335
he can transform himself into
the most hideous creatures ever seen.

868
01:11:50.416 --> 01:11:53.249
I will take the first watch at the entrance.

869
01:11:59.696 --> 01:12:03.086
You know, I have no problem
dating an older woman.

870
01:12:05.856 --> 01:12:08.086
I'm afraid we can't be together.

871
01:12:08.976 --> 01:12:11.444
Wait. What? Why?

872
01:12:13.096 --> 01:12:15.530
Because I'm going to live forever.

873
01:12:16.256 --> 01:12:18.486
I don't want to watch you die.

874
01:12:19.376 --> 01:12:21.173
So what? That's it?

875
01:12:22.096 --> 01:12:25.008
You're just gonna sit
on the sidelines for eternity?

876
01:12:25.096 --> 01:12:28.054
My mother has mourned
my father for centuries.

877
01:12:28.616 --> 01:12:31.210
I don't know if my heart can bear it.

878
01:12:35.696 --> 01:12:38.733
People can live an entire lifetime
in one look.

879
01:12:40.856 --> 01:12:43.245
I watch my parents do it every day.

880
01:12:46.216 --> 01:12:47.126
JONATHAN: Alex?

881
01:12:48.656 --> 01:12:51.124
Your father's awake. Get up here!

882
01:13:03.456 --> 01:13:04.650
Hello.

883
01:13:07.416 --> 01:13:10.453
If this is heaven, it looks pretty good so far.

884
01:13:18.336 --> 01:13:20.804
Nice to see some things never change.

885
01:13:38.176 --> 01:13:40.565
Go easy on him. He feels terrible.

886
01:13:46.016 --> 01:13:48.405
When I saw you lying there, Dad...

887
01:13:48.736 --> 01:13:51.489
I've never been so scared in my life.

888
01:13:53.016 --> 01:13:55.166
Well, that makes two of us.

889
01:13:56.176 --> 01:13:59.009
I mean, you know,
you're not supposed to die, you know?

890
01:13:59.096 --> 01:14:01.052
You're Ricochet O'Connell, right?

891
01:14:01.136 --> 01:14:04.253
You get beat up, you get tossed around,

892
01:14:04.336 --> 01:14:06.850
but, well, you're always standing there
in the end.

893
01:14:06.936 --> 01:14:10.008
I never really thought of
the world without you.

894
01:14:13.536 --> 01:14:14.935
Alex,

895
01:14:16.816 --> 01:14:18.488
the truth is,

896
01:14:20.856 --> 01:14:22.528
I'm just trying to...

897
01:14:24.536 --> 01:14:26.413
I'm just...

898
01:14:26.496 --> 01:14:27.645
I'm trying to be a good husband.

899
01:14:27.736 --> 01:14:29.055
I'm trying to be a good parent.

900
01:14:29.136 --> 01:14:32.572
And the truth is,
I've been dropping the ball lately, and...

901
01:14:32.656 --> 01:14:35.489
No, you know, I haven't been
the world's greatest son, you know?

902
01:14:35.576 --> 01:14:39.455
No, no, that's 'cause you get it
from her side of the family.

903
01:14:39.536 --> 01:14:40.855
Come here.

904
01:14:44.376 --> 01:14:45.650
My boys.

905
01:14:48.936 --> 01:14:49.971
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

906
01:14:50.056 --> 01:14:52.775
You look tired, you should rest.

907
01:14:53.736 --> 01:14:54.851
I'll stay.

908
01:14:55.976 --> 01:14:58.046
Fate is about to deal its final hand.

909
01:14:58.376 --> 01:15:00.526
If we are to defeat the Emperor...

910
01:15:00.856 --> 01:15:04.326
I must ask for one more sacrifice.

911
01:15:04.736 --> 01:15:05.930
Anything, mother.

912
01:15:07.776 --> 01:15:09.767
Your immortality.

913
01:15:13.096 --> 01:15:14.085
(EXPLOSION)

914
01:15:21.256 --> 01:15:23.770
Oh, no! His powers have been fully restored!

915
01:15:23.856 --> 01:15:25.130
Time to go.

916
01:15:46.696 --> 01:15:47.685
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

917
01:15:47.776 --> 01:15:50.051
General Ming's daughter.

918
01:15:50.856 --> 01:15:53.086
Your child will be mine.

919
01:16:01.536 --> 01:16:03.447
He is immortal.

920
01:16:30.976 --> 01:16:34.093
Hey! You three-headed shape-shifting
son of a bitch!

921
01:16:42.496 --> 01:16:44.293
(LIN GRUNTING)

922
01:16:44.376 --> 01:16:45.365
Lin!

923
01:16:55.896 --> 01:16:57.090
LIN: Alex!

924
01:17:00.576 --> 01:17:01.611
Alex!

925
01:17:10.416 --> 01:17:12.532
He's taking her back to his tomb
to raise his army!

926
01:17:12.616 --> 01:17:15.608
- Is there a faster way down from here?
- The yeti. They'll help.

927
01:17:15.696 --> 01:17:17.687
But he's already in the air. It'll be too late!

928
01:17:17.776 --> 01:17:21.769
Mad Dog can outfly a three-headed lizard
any day of the week! Let's go.

929
01:17:26.936 --> 01:17:28.767
MAGUIRE: Portside! Nine o'clock!

930
01:17:35.696 --> 01:17:38.256
Rick? Should I quit drinking?

931
01:17:43.896 --> 01:17:44.885
<i>OVER RADIO: Jonathan to Rick.</i>

932
01:17:44.976 --> 01:17:46.887
<i>You'd better get a move on if</i>
<i>you're gonna beat him to the tomb!</i>

933
01:17:46.976 --> 01:17:49.570
RICK: Yeah, yeah, just get back here as fast
as you can with the reinforcements.

934
01:17:49.656 --> 01:17:51.328
No sightseeing!

935
01:17:53.776 --> 01:17:55.448
Here, Dad.

936
01:17:55.536 --> 01:17:56.525
- Is that for me?
- Yeah.

937
01:17:56.616 --> 01:17:57.731
Nice.

938
01:17:58.496 --> 01:18:02.330
The Terracotta Army is not indestructible
until it crosses the Great Wall.

939
01:18:02.416 --> 01:18:05.647
That's comforting. How exactly are we
supposed to fend them off?

940
01:18:05.736 --> 01:18:06.930
When the Emperor built the Wall,

941
01:18:07.016 --> 01:18:08.335
he buried his enemies underneath it

942
01:18:08.416 --> 01:18:10.725
and cursed their souls
to hold it up for eternity.

943
01:18:10.816 --> 01:18:15.526
Most of them were conquered soldiers.
I will call them to battle once again.

944
01:18:15.616 --> 01:18:20.895
Unlock an altar, raise an army.
That sounds like a plan. Let's go.

945
01:18:30.336 --> 01:18:32.691
(SOLDIERS SHOUTING)

946
01:18:45.656 --> 01:18:46.645
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

947
01:18:46.736 --> 01:18:47.851
Grab her.

948
01:18:48.536 --> 01:18:50.174
Guard her with your life.

949
01:18:53.136 --> 01:18:54.285
Alex?

950
01:18:56.496 --> 01:18:58.964
- Where'd he go?
- Where do you think?

951
01:19:14.936 --> 01:19:15.925
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

952
01:19:16.016 --> 01:19:17.574
AWAKE!

953
01:20:01.616 --> 01:20:03.095
(HORSE NEIGHING)

954
01:20:49.856 --> 01:20:51.892
Today you awake to a world...

955
01:20:52.616 --> 01:20:54.891
in the grip of chaos and corruption.

956
01:20:54.976 --> 01:20:56.967
Open the gates of the past

957
01:20:57.056 --> 01:20:59.490
and free the souls
of the wrongfully damned.

958
01:21:00.176 --> 01:21:01.973
I will restore order...

959
01:21:02.656 --> 01:21:04.851
I will retake what is mine.

960
01:21:05.536 --> 01:21:08.050
I will crush any idea of freedom.

961
01:21:08.176 --> 01:21:11.168
In the name of the ancestors
and the righteous,

962
01:21:11.256 --> 01:21:14.487
I sacrifice my immortality
and that of my daughter

963
01:21:14.576 --> 01:21:16.373
so that you may rise this day!

964
01:21:16.496 --> 01:21:18.293
I will slaughter without mercy.

965
01:21:18.616 --> 01:21:21.005
I will conquer without compassion.

966
01:21:21.336 --> 01:21:23.566
I will now lead you past the Great Wall.

967
01:21:23.936 --> 01:21:27.372
Once you cross, you will be indestructible.

968
01:21:28.296 --> 01:21:33.245
Bring down the wrath of the oppressed
on this Emperor and all who follow him!

969
01:21:33.736 --> 01:21:35.772
I raised you for one purpose...

970
01:21:36.056 --> 01:21:38.695
to enforce my will on the entire world!

971
01:21:39.336 --> 01:21:40.735
Long live the Emperor!

972
01:21:43.216 --> 01:21:46.447
I call upon the hundreds and the thousands

973
01:21:46.536 --> 01:21:51.212
that you may rise up and seize this moment
to take your victory,

974
01:21:51.296 --> 01:21:54.925
to take your justice
and to take your revenge!

975
01:22:13.176 --> 01:22:14.655
Zi Yuan.

976
01:22:18.736 --> 01:22:20.692
(SHOUTING)

977
01:22:20.776 --> 01:22:22.289
It's General Ming!

978
01:22:22.736 --> 01:22:24.294
Follow General Ming!

979
01:22:28.416 --> 01:22:31.408
Prepare for battle!

980
01:22:40.296 --> 01:22:43.094
These are...
They're good undead guys, right?

981
01:22:43.656 --> 01:22:46.568
Oh, no, no, no!

982
01:22:46.656 --> 01:22:48.851
Zi Yuan! Zi Yuan! Zi Yuan sent us!

983
01:22:48.936 --> 01:22:53.009
- Darling, I don't think he speaks English.
- RICK: We're with Zi Yuan!

984
01:22:53.096 --> 01:22:54.324
Zi Yuan?

985
01:22:54.856 --> 01:22:56.050
Right.

986
01:22:57.656 --> 01:22:58.884
Let's go.

987
01:22:59.856 --> 01:23:01.130
To battle!

988
01:23:05.176 --> 01:23:08.213
(GRUNTING)

989
01:23:20.856 --> 01:23:24.815
Freedom! Freedom! Freedom!

990
01:23:27.536 --> 01:23:29.049
Archers form up!

991
01:23:33.096 --> 01:23:34.324
Incoming!

992
01:23:47.056 --> 01:23:51.015
- Hey! That's my favourite blue shirt.
- I've always hated that shirt.

993
01:23:51.096 --> 01:23:53.291
(CHATTERING)

994
01:24:05.536 --> 01:24:06.525
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

995
01:24:06.616 --> 01:24:08.174
Death to General Ming!

996
01:24:12.016 --> 01:24:13.335
Charge!

997
01:24:23.136 --> 01:24:25.172
Welcome to the 20th century!

998
01:24:25.296 --> 01:24:27.935
(MACHINE GUN FIRING)

999
01:24:40.256 --> 01:24:41.245
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1000
01:24:41.336 --> 01:24:43.691
We can't let them cross the wall!

1001
01:25:16.216 --> 01:25:18.172
(GRUNTING)

1002
01:26:06.856 --> 01:26:08.209
You are no longer immortal.

1003
01:26:47.536 --> 01:26:50.175
Honey! Fall back to higher ground!

1004
01:26:56.576 --> 01:26:58.806
I really hate mummies!

1005
01:26:58.896 --> 01:27:01.126
It seems the feeling's mutual!

1006
01:27:04.736 --> 01:27:06.772
Shut up, clay boy! Fore!

1007
01:27:07.376 --> 01:27:08.491
Run!

1008
01:27:20.896 --> 01:27:22.409
- Catch!
- Got it!

1009
01:27:24.376 --> 01:27:28.574
Next time I say, "We've been in tougher
scrapes than this," I mean this!

1010
01:27:47.056 --> 01:27:49.524
(GUN FIRING)

1011
01:27:53.176 --> 01:27:56.373
Die, you mummy bastards! Die!

1012
01:27:56.456 --> 01:27:59.368
There is no call for bad language!

1013
01:28:01.536 --> 01:28:04.653
Jonathan certainly knows
how to make an entrance!

1014
01:28:30.176 --> 01:28:31.894
Any regrets, darling?

1015
01:28:33.936 --> 01:28:35.813
None. Not ever.

1016
01:28:44.856 --> 01:28:47.654
- You okay?
- Yeah, sure, no problem.

1017
01:28:47.736 --> 01:28:50.125
We had it completely under control.

1018
01:28:52.856 --> 01:28:55.450
This guy ever run out of tricks?

1019
01:28:59.656 --> 01:29:00.930
No!

1020
01:29:07.856 --> 01:29:09.289
Mother! No!

1021
01:29:12.016 --> 01:29:13.244
Mother!

1022
01:29:17.976 --> 01:29:20.171
Mother! Mother!

1023
01:29:30.056 --> 01:29:31.967
Pierce through his heart.

1024
01:29:34.696 --> 01:29:39.008
You must live and fight on.

1025
01:29:39.816 --> 01:29:41.534
(CRYING)

1026
01:29:57.616 --> 01:30:00.084
She said through the heart.

1027
01:30:00.176 --> 01:30:02.610
Through the heart. Let's go.

1028
01:30:14.856 --> 01:30:15.845
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1029
01:30:15.936 --> 01:30:16.971
Get in!

1030
01:30:17.816 --> 01:30:20.410
The O'Connells are going to
stop the Emperor!

1031
01:30:31.576 --> 01:30:33.885
So, Dad, what's the plan?

1032
01:30:33.976 --> 01:30:35.409
Divide and conquer!

1033
01:30:35.496 --> 01:30:38.454
No offence,
but isn't that a little short on detail?

1034
01:30:39.136 --> 01:30:41.525
- Twelve o'clock low!
- Hang on!

1035
01:30:49.456 --> 01:30:50.809
Remember our deal!

1036
01:30:50.896 --> 01:30:53.410
When this is over,
my men get to drink for free!

1037
01:30:53.496 --> 01:30:56.294
You can have the whole damn bar
for all I care!

1038
01:30:56.376 --> 01:30:58.970
I'm getting the hell out of China.

1039
01:31:28.416 --> 01:31:29.405
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1040
01:31:29.496 --> 01:31:31.851
I dug you up...

1041
01:31:32.736 --> 01:31:35.091
and I'm gonna put you down.

1042
01:31:49.256 --> 01:31:51.406
(SCREAMING)

1043
01:32:05.136 --> 01:32:07.775
Alex? Alex!

1044
01:32:27.496 --> 01:32:29.134
(GRUNTING)

1045
01:32:34.096 --> 01:32:35.893
(CHOKING)

1046
01:33:04.216 --> 01:33:05.205
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1047
01:33:05.296 --> 01:33:06.331
Let go!

1048
01:33:06.416 --> 01:33:07.451
Never!

1049
01:33:11.216 --> 01:33:14.049
RICK: Enough tricks! Where's your honour?

1050
01:33:17.056 --> 01:33:18.694
Fight like a man!

1051
01:33:24.456 --> 01:33:26.287
(RICK GRUNTING)

1052
01:33:55.856 --> 01:33:57.448
Divide

1053
01:33:58.976 --> 01:34:00.375
and conquer.

1054
01:34:38.336 --> 01:34:40.452
(EMPEROR GROANING)

1055
01:34:45.136 --> 01:34:47.855
Now you can rule in hell.

1056
01:35:12.056 --> 01:35:13.045
(SPEAKING MANDARIN)

1057
01:35:13.136 --> 01:35:14.808
The Emperor is dead.

1058
01:35:15.096 --> 01:35:16.688
The Emperor is dead!

1059
01:35:51.816 --> 01:35:54.125
(SINGING)

1060
01:36:01.696 --> 01:36:05.655
- Evening, girls. You're looking well.
- WOMAN: Good evening, Mr Maguire.

1061
01:36:06.496 --> 01:36:10.125
- It's a fine night to be me.
- You dance great for an old lady.

1062
01:36:10.656 --> 01:36:13.090
Someone told me to stop living
on the sidelines.

1063
01:36:13.176 --> 01:36:16.088
- Well, he sounds like a smart guy.
- He is.

1064
01:36:27.616 --> 01:36:30.972
So I guess Dash and Scarlet
have their next adventure?

1065
01:36:31.056 --> 01:36:33.809
Why write about it when you can live it?

1066
01:36:34.896 --> 01:36:38.935
There's something incredibly romantic
about vanquishing the undead.

1067
01:36:39.736 --> 01:36:42.204
Even more romantic doing it with you.

1068
01:36:42.976 --> 01:36:45.695
- Kiss me.
- Don't have to ask me twice.

1069
01:36:54.456 --> 01:36:56.048
- Can I get your bag, sir?
- No, no, no.

1070
01:36:56.136 --> 01:36:58.047
Don't touch it, don't touch it.

1071
01:36:58.136 --> 01:36:59.125
Where are you off to, Mr Carnahan?

1072
01:36:59.216 --> 01:37:01.491
Someplace where they don't have mummies.

1073
01:37:01.576 --> 01:37:04.295
- Step on it! I've got a plane to catch.
- DRIVER: Yes, sir.

1074
01:37:04.376 --> 01:37:07.891
Yeah. <i>Ciao, ciao,</i> Shanghai.

1075
01:37:07.976 --> 01:37:10.007
Peru,
here I come.

1076
01:37:12.936 --> 01:37:17.214
Soon after, mummies were found in Peru.

1077
01:47:02.256 --> 01:47:03.245
